'''Jacan Baliscans''' ({{Langx|an|xacano-baliscanos}}; {{langx|bl|jacano-baliscanos}}) refers to [[Baliscans|Baliscan]] citizens of full or partial [[Jacan|Jacano]] ancestry or those born in the [[W:Autonomous communities of Spain|historical region]] of [[W:Aragon|Aragon]] in [[western Illypnia]] who reside in [[Balisca]]. Aragonese Baliscans form one of the largest [[Illypnian Baliscans|Illypnian ancestry]] groups in the confederation. Between 1857 and 1936, an estimated 1,261,000 Jacano people immigrated to Balisca, predominately settling in [[Bayara]]. 

Baliscans of Jacano descent make up a substantial proportion of the Baliscan population, and have historically played an integral role in the socioeconomic development of the [[Northern Triangle]], particularly in Bayara.

